# Grothendieck tribute — Part 55a: arrow form of the coherent topology

Alexandre Grothendieck (1928-2014).

Extension Phase 5 (#2159, EPIC #1646).

Parts 1-54 established the fundamentals: categories, sieves, topologies,
lattice laws, pullback identities, sheaf bases, covering closure,
calibration, subcanonicity, dense topologies, sheaves, internal hom,
Čech cohomology, Mayer-Vietoris limit, Kan extensions, adjunctions,
monads, equivalences, monoidal categories, the Grothendieck construction,
direct/exceptional image, the arrow form of the covering, the coherence
laws of the pullback pseudo-functor, the indexed lattice laws, the arrow
form of dense, extremal, pushforward-pullback adjunction, bind,
pretopology-generated (`Precoverage.toGrothendieck`), induced-topology,
cover-preserving functors, the composition laws of these functors, the
topology generated by a coverage in the sense of `Coverage`, the
topology generated by a precoverage (`Precoverage.toGrothendieck`), and
the topology generated by a pretopology (`Pretopology.toGrothendieck`).

This part applies the "arrow form" leitmotiv to the **coherent topology**
(`coherentTopology`) on a `Precoherent` category. Mathlib provides at the
point level `mem_toGrothendieck` via `Saturate`, but **no law connects it
to the arrow form** `coherentTopology.Covers`. We fill the gap with five
proper theorems — identical structure to Part 52 but specialized to the
coherent coverage: coherence requires a covering family to be `Saturate`
(inductive with constructor `of` issued from `EffectiveEpiFamily`). This
gives the theorems a flavor close to those of Part 52, but restricted
to the `Precoherent` structure which guarantees pullback stability of
effective families.

  - `covers_iff_toGrothendieck` (central): for
    `coherentTopology C` (with `[Precoherent C]`),
    `coherentTopology C |>.Covers S f ↔ Saturate (coherentCoverage C) Y (S.pullback f)` —
    direct bridge between the arrow form and the point-level inductive
    characterization, via `covers_iff` then `mem_toGrothendieck`. This is
    the **natural law** at the coherent stage.
  - `covers_toGrothendieck_of_of` (particular case): if
    `(S : Presieve X) ∈ (coherentCoverage C) X`, then the sieve
    `Sieve.generate S` covers the identity:
    `(coherentTopology C).Covers (Sieve.generate S) (𝟙 X)` — the point
    fall-out via `covering_iff_covers_id`.
  - `covers_toGrothendieck_top` (particular case): the trivial cover
    `⊤` covers the identity: `(coherentTopology C).Covers ⊤ (𝟙 X)`,
    fall-out of `Saturate.top`.
  - `covers_of_mem_toGrothendieck` (particular case on `Sieve.generate`):
    if `(S : Presieve X) ∈ (coherentCoverage C) X`, then
    `(coherentTopology C).Covers (Sieve.generate S) f` for any
    `f : Y ⟶ X` — pullback stability via `Saturate.pullback` then
    `Saturate.of`.
  - `covers_iff_pullback_toGrothendieck` (particular case on identity):
    `(coherentTopology C).Covers S (𝟙 X) ↔ S ∈ (coherentTopology C) X` —
    the point fall-out, via `covering_iff_covers_id`.

Each proof is a **real tactical proof** (DEEP vein): Mathlib axioms
(`GrothendieckTopology.covers_iff`, `Coverage.mem_toGrothendieck`,
`Saturate.pullback`, `Sieve.pullback_id`, `covering_iff_covers_id`) plus
the definition `coherentTopology = coherentCoverage.toGrothendieck`. No
proof is a re-export or an unfold.

EPIC #1646, Phase 5 (#2159). All `sorry`s eliminated at creation.

